Atlas Farm Taroudant – Customized Enterprise Development Blueprint
Large diversified farm
 B2C + B2B
 AI-powered


Based on your decisions, I recommend building Atlas Farm Taroudant as a modular Agricultural ERP + E-commerce + AI platform, rather than a conventional website with an admin panel.

The distinction is important: a large diversified farm needs to manage several interconnected business activities:
- Livestock and animal breeding.
- Dairy production and processing.
- Crop cultivation and harvesting.
- Agricultural products and seasonal sales.
- Purchasing and supplier relationships.
- Inventory and warehouses.
- Wholesale and retail customers.
- Transportation and distribution.
- Employees and operational expenses.
- Financial performance and forecasting.
All these activities should share one central database.
1. The customized business architecture








academieagriculture.com


The platform will have five interconnected systems
ATLAS FARM TAROUDANT
Unified agricultural business ecosystem

Commerce
Online store, livestock marketplace, wholesale and customer portal

Farm ERP
Livestock, dairy, crops, production and inventory

Business management
Accounting, procurement, HR and operations

Distribution
Warehouses, deliveries, routes and logistics


AI and Business Intelligence
Forecasting, optimization, decision support and automation

Central data platform
PostgreSQL · APIs · Permissions · Integrations · Audit logs

The most important architectural principle is that the systems must communicate.

For example:

A customer orders 100 litres of milk → the order reserves available stock → the dairy module checks production and inventory → the delivery module schedules transportation → the financial module records revenue → the analytics module updates performance indicators.

This should happen automatically through controlled business workflows.

2. Customized module specification
I recommend 12 main operational modules.
Module 1 – Livestock and animal management








ppb.projectprofilebd.com


This module should manage the complete animal lifecycle.

Submodules:
- Animal registration and identification.
- Cattle, sheep, goats and other species.
- Breed and genetic records.
- Birth and genealogy.
- Purchasing and animal acquisition.
- Breeding and reproduction.
- Pregnancy and calving records.
- Weight monitoring.
- Feed consumption.
- Vaccination and veterinary records.
- Milk production per animal.
- Animal transfers.
- Livestock sales and mortality records.
Advanced functionality:
- QR code for every animal.
- Digital animal passport.
- Individual animal profitability.
- Breeding performance analytics.
- Health event reminders.
- Veterinary document attachments.
- Animal history timeline.
The owner should be able to scan an animal's QR code using a smartphone and immediately see its complete record.
Module 2 – Dairy production and processing








zsiron.com


Support both raw milk production and any dairy processing activities the farm actually performs.

Submodules:
- Milk production by animal.
- Morning and evening production.
- Milk collection.
- Quality control.
- Storage tanks.
- Batch identification.
- Processing records.
- Packaging.
- Finished product inventory.
- Expiration tracking.
- Distribution.
Critical calculations:
\[
\text{Milk Balance} =
\text{Opening Stock}+\text{Production}
-\text{Sales}-\text{Processing}-\text{Losses}
\]

Track production costs per litre and profitability by dairy product.

For food safety, include temperature monitoring, hygiene records, batch traceability, and configurable quality-control procedures.
Module 3 – Crop and agricultural production management








fr.le360.ma


This is particularly important because the farm is diversified.

Manage different crops, fields, orchards and growing seasons.

Submodules:
- Field and plot registration.
- Field boundaries and maps.
- Crop planning.
- Planting and harvesting.
- Irrigation schedules.
- Fertilizer applications.
- Pesticide application records.
- Soil analysis.
- Weather information.
- Agricultural equipment.
- Harvest quantity.
- Crop quality.
- Agricultural production costs.
Example crop records:
Crop	Data tracked
Citrus	Area, variety, yield and harvest
Olives	Trees, yield and harvest
Vegetables	Planting cycles and production
Cereals	Field area and yield
Other crops	Configurable crop records

Do not assume the farm grows these crops; make every crop category configurable.
Smart irrigation and water management
Given the agricultural environment around Taroudant, I would make water management a priority.

Features:
- Water consumption per field.
- Irrigation schedules.
- Pump operating hours.
- Water costs.
- Soil moisture sensor integration.
- Weather-based irrigation recommendations.
- Water consumption analytics.
- Alerts for unusual consumption.
AI recommendations should be advisory and based on available soil, crop and weather data.
Module 4 – Product manufacturing and processing
If the farm transforms raw agricultural materials into finished products, include a lightweight manufacturing module.

For example:
- Raw milk → pasteurized milk, if the farm is equipped and authorized.
- Raw milk → cheese or yogurt.
- Olives → olive oil.
- Agricultural crops → packaged products.
Features:
- Production recipes.
- Bills of materials.
- Raw material consumption.
- Production batches.
- Labor and processing costs.
- Finished products.
- Waste and losses.
- Batch traceability.
This makes it possible to calculate the actual cost of manufacturing each finished product.
